0..56 Comment "//! No case tells two constants apart that a rule joins."
57..60 Comment "//!"
61..136 Comment "//! A rule that joins two constants makes them one value. A case that gives"
137..213 Comment "//! them two answers gives one value two answers. A pair of rules that sends"
214..269 Comment "//! each constant to the other one has no last rewrite."
270..273 Comment "//!"
274..352 Comment "//! The checker refuses a case whose arms differ on the two sides of the rule."
353..431 Comment "//! It refuses a case with no arm for the two joined constants. The path order"
432..508 Comment "//! refuses the pair of rules, because no order puts each constant above the"
509..523 Comment "//! other one."
524..527 Comment "//!"
528..544 Comment "//! - see: #8330"
546..558 Comment "// `Hollow`."
